    'intro'  => '<p>Durham is a former tobacco and textile city that has become one of the Triangle&rsquo;s most dynamic places to live. <strong>Duke University</strong> and <strong>Duke University Hospital</strong> are its largest institutions, <strong>North Carolina Central University</strong> anchors the south side of downtown, and old warehouses at Brightleaf Square and the American Tobacco Campus now hold offices, restaurants and apartments.</p><p>Short-term demand here is driven as much by medicine and research as by students. Duke Health brings residents, visiting physicians, travel nurses and research staff year-round, and Research Triangle Park, just southeast of the city, pulls in summer interns and relocating employees. Duke students who leave for the summer or study abroad add furnished rooms around Trinity Park, Ninth Street and Old West Durham.</p><p>A furnished sublet is a practical way to try out Durham before signing a lease, especially if you are deciding between Durham, Chapel Hill and Raleigh. Downtown and the neighborhoods around East Campus are walkable; most of the rest of the city is easier with a car.</p>',
