  'in/bloomington' => [
    'name'   => 'Bloomington',
    'state'  => 'IN',
    'type'   => 'college',
    'lat'    => 39.1653, 'lng' => -86.5264,
    'tagline'=> 'Furnished sublets near Indiana University, Kirkwood Avenue and the courthouse square in southern Indiana&rsquo;s hill country.',
    'intro'  => '<p>Bloomington is a hilly, wooded college town in southern Indiana and the home of <strong>Indiana University Bloomington</strong>, the flagship campus of IU. Kirkwood Avenue links the limestone campus to the historic courthouse square, and the surrounding neighborhoods mix student houses, faculty homes and small apartment buildings.</p><p>The short-term market is tied tightly to IU&rsquo;s calendar. After spring semester ends in early May, many students leave town and sublet their furnished rooms through the summer, which suits summer session students, Jacobs School of Music summer programs, visiting researchers and interns. During the school year, students leaving for an overseas program or an internship elsewhere hand off rooms for a single semester.</p><p>Outside the university calendar, <strong>IU Health Bloomington Hospital</strong> brings clinicians and travel nurses to town year-round, and IU&rsquo;s medical education programs place students here for clinical training. Bloomington is about an hour from Indianapolis, and some residents commute or travel there regularly.</p>',
