      ['name' => 'West Urbana', 'blurb' => 'Leafy residential neighborhood east of campus with older homes, popular with faculty and grad students.'],
      ['name' => 'Midtown Champaign', 'blurb' => 'Between campus and downtown Champaign, with newer apartments and easy access to both.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>As a hedged, rough guide, a furnished room in Champaign-Urbana might cost about <strong>$500&ndash;$950 per month</strong>, and a furnished studio or one-bedroom roughly <strong>$900&ndash;$1,600+</strong>. New high-rises in Campustown typically charge the most.</p><p>With so many Campustown units vacated for the summer, May-to-August sublets can go well below the regular lease rate. Expect that discount to shrink for fall-semester stays or for places right on Green Street; check what comparable current listings charge before you commit.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p>The <strong>Champaign-Urbana Mass Transit District (MTD)</strong> runs an extensive bus network across both cities and campus. <strong>Illinois Terminal</strong> in downtown Champaign is the hub for MTD buses, intercity buses and Amtrak trains to Chicago and beyond.</p><p><strong>University of Illinois Willard Airport (CMI)</strong> has limited flights, and many travelers use Chicago airports, reachable by train or bus. Many residents live without a car near campus.</p>',
