    'tagline'=> 'Furnished sublets near Texas A&amp;M, Northgate and downtown Bryan in the Brazos Valley.',
    'intro'  => '<p>College Station and its neighbor Bryan form one of the fastest-growing areas in Texas, built around <strong>Texas A&amp;M University</strong>. The campus dominates daily life, from game days at Kyle Field to the student apartments that ring the university.</p><p>Much of the off-campus housing is in large, purpose-built student complexes, and many residents sublet their furnished units from May to August rather than pay for an empty room. Co-op terms and study abroad free up units during the school year as well. Visiting researchers, summer interns, Texas A&amp;M Health students and people relocating to the Brazos Valley use those places.</p><p>Two hospital systems keep clinical demand steady: <strong>Baylor Scott &amp; White Medical Center &ndash; College Station</strong> and <strong>CHI St. Joseph Health</strong> in Bryan draw travel nurses and clinicians. The area is car-dependent outside campus, and summers are hot, so look for places with reliable air conditioning and parking. Asking a leaseholder for a May-to-August sublease is often easier than finding a short lease directly from a complex.</p>',
    'neighborhoods' => [
      ['name' => 'Northgate', 'blurb' => 'Dense student area north of campus with bars, restaurants and apartments; walkable to classes.'],
      ['name' => 'Southside', 'blurb' => 'Historic neighborhood south of campus with older homes and some rentals; quieter than Northgate.'],
      ['name' => 'Wolf Pen Creek', 'blurb' => 'Area with apartments, shops and an amphitheater east of campus; convenient for students and young professionals.'],
      ['name' => 'Downtown Bryan', 'blurb' => 'Revitalized historic downtown with lofts, restaurants and music venues; a short drive from campus.'],
      ['name' => 'Southwood Valley', 'blurb' => 'Residential neighborhood in south College Station with single-family homes; good for longer stays.'],
    ],
    'prices' => '<p>As a hedged, rough guide, a furnished room in College Station might cost about <strong>$500&ndash;$950 per month</strong>, and a furnished studio or one-bedroom roughly <strong>$900&ndash;$1,600+</strong>. Newer complexes with amenities near campus usually cost more.</p><p>Summer is when complexes fill with subleasers competing for tenants, so it is usually the easiest time to negotiate. Anything overlapping a home game at Kyle Field or the August rush costs more; ask whether a complex charges a sublease or transfer fee, and compare current listings.</p>',
    'transit'=> '<p><strong>Texas A&amp;M Transportation Services</strong> runs extensive campus and off-campus bus routes during the semester, and the <strong>Brazos Transit District</strong> provides regional bus service. Many student apartment complexes are on A&amp;M bus routes.</p><p><strong>Easterwood Airport (CLL)</strong> has limited flights; Houston airports are roughly a 90-minute to two-hour drive. Plan on a car for errands, the hospitals and trips to Houston or Austin.</p>',
    'tips' => [
      'interns'  => 'Summer interns can find good-value furnished units in student complexes from May through August. Ask whether A&amp;M buses run on a reduced summer schedule near your place.',
      'nurses'   => 'Travel nurses typically work at <strong>Baylor Scott &amp; White Medical Center &ndash; College Station</strong> or <strong>CHI St. Joseph Health Regional Hospital</strong> in Bryan. South College Station and Bryan neighborhoods keep commutes short.',
      'students' => 'Students at <strong>Texas A&amp;M University</strong> and <strong>Blinn College</strong> sublet for summer, co-ops or study abroad. Texas A&amp;M Health students on rotations often look for furnished places near the medical corridor.',
      'seasonal' => 'Subleases pile up in May as the spring semester closes. Game weekends at Kyle Field are the hardest time to book a short stay, along with commencement ceremonies and the August move-in rush.',
    ],
